-- emit: the derived `eq` of a NOMINAL type, one line per constructor shape
-- (`docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §9.4, §8.5, A.18, A.20, A.23).
--
-- **The golden is §9's SHAPE, not its listing.** §9.4's and §9.6's worked
-- examples name the two operands `x` and `y` and the nominal function
-- `<Type>$eq`; the emitter writes `$x`, `$y` and `<Type>$$eq`, because a
-- derived body's operands share a namespace with the module's own locals
-- and the nominal base has to be one no module path can spell (§8.5). The
-- structure — which positions are compared, in what order, and what a tag
-- test does — is the spec's; the spelling is this file's, and only the
-- spelling.
--
-- Five shapes, and the golden is where their differences are visible:
--
--   - `Colour` is all-nullary, so its values are bare tag strings and `eq`
--     is `===` with nothing to walk (A.18). The row is emitted anyway,
--     because another module may name it as evidence.
--   - `Metre` has one constructor, so there is no tag test and no `switch`:
--     nothing to disagree about.
--   - `Shape` has two of DIFFERENT arity, so every constructor is padded to
--     the widest and the `switch` touches only the arguments the live one
--     has. The padding slots are not compared (A.12), and the LAST
--     constructor is the `default` arm with no `case` of its own.
--   - `Tree` is recursive: a top-level `const` arrow may name itself from
--     inside its body, so the derived function simply calls itself.
--   - `Box a` is parametric: one evidence parameter per type PARAMETER, in
--     declaration order, and a position that is the parameter is that
--     parameter applied (A.20).
--
-- Every one of them is emitted although this module compares only two:
-- derivation for a nominal type is EAGER and happens in the declaring
-- module (A.23, §8.5), so they are exported as well.
import Node exposing (Program)


pub type Colour
    = Red
    | Green
    | Blue


pub type Metre
    = Metre Float


pub type Shape
    = Circle Float
    | Rect Float Float


pub type Tree
    = Leaf
    | Node Tree Int Tree


pub type Box a
    = Box a


pub sameShape : Shape, Shape -> Bool
sameShape a b =
    a == b


pub sameTree : Tree, Tree -> Bool
sameTree a b =
    a == b


pub sameBoxes : Box Int, Box Int -> Bool
sameBoxes a b =
    a == b


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines []
